                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "238795391",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561198153489786",
                            "num_reviews": 55,
                            "playtime_forever": 1102,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 392,
                            "playtime_at_review": 1102,
                            "last_played": 1793249365
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "SPOILER ALERT, unspoil only if you think the game is terrible/you've finished playing the game.\n\n[spoiler]I too thought the game was terrible until I played the later routes, those that only unlock after doing the early routes. I discovered - much to my surprise - that the early routes were intentionally maddening loops that set the stage for the real main characters. The reason why the early routes seem so stiff and wooden is because they are. It's by design, and it pissed me off. Still, this mad writing method paid off - the ending wouldn't've hit as hard as it did without all the loops it took to reach it. The final hidden route with Zhenya moved me! Don't play Zhenya's route until you've played all the others in proper sequence, please trust me on this. It was a truly satisfying conclusion to an insane story that made all the frustration worth it.\n\n...Lena's still a nutcase though; stay away from a knife-wielding woman gentlemen, you can't fix her.\n[/spoiler]",
